{"slug": "rhubarb-crisp", "nyt_id": 1013147, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1013147-rhubarb-crisp", "name": "Rhubarb Crisp", "author": "Mark Bittman", "description": "When you think of rhubarb you probably think of strawberry-rhubarb pie, a quintessential spring dessert, especially if it’s made by someone who makes good pies. I usually manage around one pie crust annually, so I need alternatives. Thus, when the spring’s first rhubarb shows up, I adjust the execution and produce a crisp. If rhubarb is young and fresh, you can trim it in seconds. If it has fibrous outer strings, peel them off as you would those of celery. Toss the rhubarb with orange or lemon juice and zest, and only a little sugar. (You can also substitute strawberries for some of the rhubarb if you want the classic combination.) Blend the ingredients for the crisp topping in a food processor, crumble the topping over the rhubarb mixture, and bake — it is nearly effortless and as good or better than a pie.", "servings": {"text": "6 to 8 servings", "min": 6, "max": 8, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 60, "raw": {"total": "PT1H"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "6 tablespoons cold butter, cut into small pieces, plus more for greasing pan", "group": null, "quantity": 6.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "cold butter", "preparation": "cut into small pieces, plus more for greasing pan", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "2 ½ to 3 pounds rhubarb, trimmed, tough strings removed, and cut into 1 ½-inch pieces (about 5 to 6 cups)", "group": null, "quantity": 2.5, "unit": "lb", "item": "rhubarb", "preparation": "trimmed, tough strings removed, and cut into 1 ½-inch pieces (about 5 to 6 cups)", "optional": false, "quantity_max": 3.0}, {"position": 3, "raw": "¼ cup white sugar", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "cup", "item": "white sugar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "1 tablespoon orange or lemon juice", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "orange or lemon juice", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "1 teaspoon orange or lemon zest", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tsp", "item": "orange or lemon zest", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "¾ cup brown sugar", "group": null, "quantity": 0.75, "unit": "cup", "item": "brown sugar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "½ cup all-purpose flour", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "all-purpose flour", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "½ teaspoon cinnamon, or to taste", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "tsp", "item": "cinnamon", "preparation": "or to taste", "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "Pinch salt", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "pinch salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "½ cup rolled oats", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "rolled oats", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "½ cup pecans", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "pecans", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Heat oven to 375 degrees. Grease an 8- or 9-inch square baking or gratin dish with a little butter. Toss rhubarb with white sugar, orange or lemon juice and zest, and spread in baking dish."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Put the 6 tablespoons butter in a food processor along with brown sugar, flour, cinnamon and salt, and pulse for about 20 or 30 seconds, until it looks like small peas and just begins to clump together. Add oats and pecans and pulse just a few times to combine."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Crumble the topping over rhubarb and bake until golden and beginning to brown, 45 to 50 minutes."}], "nutrition": {"source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "calories": 275.625, "protein_g": 3.6, "carbohydrates_g": 37.2, "fat_g": 13.8, "saturated_fat_g": 5.9, "unsaturated_fat_g": 2.0, "trans_fat_g": null, "cholesterol_mg": 22.9, "sodium_mg": 30.1, "fiber_g": 4.2, "sugar_g": 21.5, "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": [], "course": ["crisp-dessert"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["food-processor", "pecan", "rhubarb", "rolled-oat", "spring"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2018/07/20/dining/bittman-rhubarb-crisp-horizontal/merlin_137567802_d4758259-042a-4b7e-8122-e634664add6d-videoSixteenByNineJumbo1600.jpg", "alt": "Mark Bittman's rhubarb crisp.", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2018/07/20/dining/bittman-rhubarb-crisp-horizontal/merlin_137567802_d4758259-042a-4b7e-8122-e634664add6d-superJumbo.jpg", "alt": "Mark Bittman's rhubarb crisp.", "primary": false}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2018/07/20/dining/bittman-rhubarb-crisp-horizontal/merlin_137567802_d4758259-042a-4b7e-8122-e634664add6d-facebookJumbo.jpg", "alt": "Mark Bittman's rhubarb crisp.", "primary": false}], "rating": {"average": 5.0, "count": 6115}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2010-05-19", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T01:43:34Z", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "rhubarb-strawberry-mousse", "nyt_id": 1013165, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1013165-rhubarb-strawberry-mousse", "name": "Rhubarb-Strawberry Mousse", "author": "Amanda Hesser", "description": "Amanda Hesser", "servings": {"text": "8 to 10 servings", "min": 8, "max": 10, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 50, "raw": {"total": "PT50M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 ¼ pounds rhubarb, finely diced", "group": null, "quantity": 1.25, "unit": "lb", "item": "rhubarb", "preparation": "finely diced", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 cup sliced strawberries", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "cup", "item": "sliced strawberries", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "1 cup sugar", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "cup", "item": "sugar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "2 tablespoons kirsch", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "kirsch", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "1 tablespoon unflavored gelatin", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "unflavored gelatin", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "2 cups heavy cream", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "cup", "item": "heavy cream", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Combine the rhubarb, strawberries and sugar in a heavy 2-quart saucepan and simmer for 20 minutes, until the rhubarb is soft."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Pour ⅔ of the mixture into a blender with the kirsch; purée and set aside."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Pour 4 tablespoons cold water into a small saucepan and sprinkle the gelatin over the top. Allow to soften for 10 minutes. Heat gently until the gelatin has completely dissolved. Stir into the rhubarb purée."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Combine the purée with the remaining cooked rhubarb mixture."}, {"position": 5, "text": "Whip the heavy cream until stiff and fold into the rhubarb mixture. Chill for several hours."}], "nutrition": {"source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "calories": 265.2, "protein_g": 2.6, "carbohydrates_g": 25.2, "fat_g": 17.3, "saturated_fat_g": 11.0, "unsaturated_fat_g": 0.8, "trans_fat_g": 0.6, "cholesterol_mg": 53.8, "sodium_mg": 16.9, "fiber_g": 1.4, "sugar_g": 22.8, "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": [], "course": ["dessert-mousse"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["spring"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2014/04/04/dining/Rhubarb-Strawberry-Mousse/Rhubarb-Strawberry-Mousse-superJumbo.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2014/04/04/dining/Rhubarb-Strawberry-Mousse/Rhubarb-Strawberry-Mousse-facebookJumbo-v2.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": false}], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 198}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2010-06-06", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T01:44:15Z", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "rhubarb-upside-down-cake", "nyt_id": 1013611, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1013611-rhubarb-upside-down-cake", "name": "Rhubarb Upside-Down Cake", "author": "Melissa Clark", "description": "Take advantage of rhubarb season with this easy dessert. Baked and unmolded, this cake resembles a pale pink mosaic atop velvet-crumbed and vanilla-infused cake. The rhubarb, which you’ll add in raw, is tangy and tender, firm enough to give you something to chew over. It’s an easy half-hour of prep and another hour and change in the oven, ample time for a light supper, anticipation of dessert hanging in the spring air.", "servings": {"text": "8 servings", "min": 8, "max": 8, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": 75, "total_minutes": 105, "raw": {"cook": "PT1H15M", "total": "PT1H45M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "2 ½ sticks unsalted butter, at room temperature, more to grease pans", "group": null, "quantity": 2.5, "unit": "stick", "item": "unsalted butter", "preparation": "at room temperature, more to grease pans", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 ½ pounds rhubarb, rinsed and sliced into ½-inch cubes about 4 cups", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "unit": "lb", "item": "rhubarb", "preparation": "rinsed and sliced into ½-inch cubes about 4 cups", "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "2 teaspoons cornstarch", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tsp", "item": "cornstarch", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "1 ½ cups granulated sugar", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "granulated sugar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "½ cup light brown sugar", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "light brown sugar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "2 cups cake flour", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "cup", "item": "cake flour", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "1 ¼ teaspoons baking powder", "group": null, "quantity": 1.25, "unit": "tsp", "item": "baking powder", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "½ teaspoon fine sea salt", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "tsp", "item": "fine sea salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "Zest of 1 lemon, grated", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "zest of 1 lemon", "preparation": "grated", "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "1 teaspoon vanilla extract", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tsp", "item": "vanilla extract", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "4 large eggs", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "unit": null, "item": "large eggs", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "⅓ cup sour cream", "group": null, "quantity": 0.3333333333333333, "unit": "cup", "item": "sour cream", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 13, "raw": "2 teaspoons lemon juice", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tsp", "item": "lemon juice", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Heat oven to 325 degrees. Line the bottom of a 9-inch springform pan with parchment paper. Butter the paper and sides of the pan. Wrap two layers of foil under the pan, and place it on a baking sheet."}, {"position": 2, "text": "In a medium bowl, mix rhubarb, cornstarch and ½ cup granulated sugar."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Mix the brown sugar and ½ stick butter in a pan over medium heat. Whisk until smooth and bubbling, about 2 minutes. Sift together the cake flour, baking powder and salt."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Whip 2 sticks butter in a mixer with a paddle attachment for 2 minutes. With your fingers, blend the remaining 1 cup sugar with lemon zest until the mixture is uniform in color. Cream together with the butter at medium-high speed until it is light and fluffy, about 4 minutes, stopping to scrape down the bowl halfway through. Add the vanilla and mix well. Add the eggs, one at a time, mixing well after each addition. Mix in the sour cream, then the lemon juice. (It’s O.K. if the mixture looks curdled.) With the mixer set to low speed, add the flour mixture, ¼ cup at a time, until well combined. Scrape down the mixer bowl in between the additions."}, {"position": 5, "text": "Pour the brown-sugar mixture into the cake pan, then spoon in the rhubarb and its juices. Spoon in the batter so it covers all of the rhubarb. Smooth out the top."}, {"position": 6, "text": "Bake for 1 hour and 15 minutes, or until the top of the cake is firm to touch and a toothpick stuck in the middle comes out without any large, moist crumbs."}, {"position": 7, "text": "Place the pan on a wire rack, and cool for 15 minutes. Run a knife around the cake, place a plate on top of the pan and turn it upside-down. Release the cake from the pan while still warm or else it will stick."}], "nutrition": {"source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "calories": 637.0, "protein_g": 7.4, "carbohydrates_g": 79.5, "fat_g": 33.4, "saturated_fat_g": 19.7, "unsaturated_fat_g": 1.8, "trans_fat_g": 0.1, "cholesterol_mg": 174.6, "sodium_mg": 251.9, "fiber_g": 2.4, "sugar_g": 48.1, "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": [], "course": ["dessert"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["cake-flour", "rhubarb", "spring"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2019/03/22/dining/mc-rhubarb-upside-down-cake/mc-rhubarb-upside-down-cake-videoSixteenByNineJumbo1600-v2.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2019/03/22/dining/mc-rhubarb-upside-down-cake/mc-rhubarb-upside-down-cake-googleFourByThree-v2.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": false}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2019/03/22/dining/mc-rhubarb-upside-down-cake/mc-rhubarb-upside-down-cake-mediumSquareAt3X-v2.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": false}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2019/03/22/dining/mc-rhubarb-upside-down-cake/mc-rhubarb-upside-down-cake-facebookJumbo-v2.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": false}], "rating": {"average": 5.0, "count": 3870}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2011-05-25", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T01:56:39Z", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
